    "body": "Requested changes applied in efde2fb1:\n\n1. **Parallels under a grip vise (blocker).** `fit_under_stock` now refuses a vise whose `seat_height() > 0` by name: \"'<vise>' is a grip-jaw vise: it seats the stock on its steps, parallels do not go under it\" (`crates/app/src/commands/accessory.rs:105-111`). Pinned by `parallels_are_refused_under_a_grip_jaw_vise` (`crates/app/tests/self_centering_grip_jaw.rs`): a stepless 80 mm self-centering vise still takes parallels, the 3 / 1.5 grip vise is refused. It fails without the fix.\n2. **Place-mode origin text.** `VisePlacement::At` doc (`crates/app/src/commands/builtin_vise.rs:27-30`) and the `add_builtin_vise` description (`crates/app/src/mcp/vise_tools.rs:25`) now say the self-centering origin is at the ledge with a grip step.\n3. **Decision note** (`docs/decisions/1274-grip-jaw.md`): records the 0 (off) defaults with the typical 3 / 1.5 in the tooltips, that `grip_width` is checked against `jaw_thickness` (the ledge is added inward of the face, so the model is never thinner than the steel), and the parallels refusal with the seat-aware fit dropped.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (app suites incl. self_centering_grip_jaw 6/6, accessory_collisions, builtin_accessory, builtin_vise, mcp_vise; ui lib/boundary/boundary_picks/theme_files); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` clean. upstream/main not merged (your trial merge was clean).\n\nReady for a re-review.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
